# UIBC golden fixtures: byte-deterministic cross-platform (archive SS32).
#
# Root cause of the #177 S4 failure: evidence files were written in Python
# text mode without `newline="\n"`, so on Windows they gained CRLF while the
# stored git blob was LF. The manifest recorded the CRLF content hash, so a
# Linux/macOS (LF) checkout failed S4 while Windows (CRLF) passed -- the same
# signature package verified differently per platform.
#
# Fix (two layers):
#   1. Generators/library now write all fixture content with newline="\n" (LF).
#   2. This attribute forces LF on BOTH store and checkout for every file under
#      fixtures/, so content hashes are identical on every platform.
fixtures/** text eol=lf
